{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test sources and did not request any implementation source. The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`.\n\n**Combining contributions and including every applicable one**\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` builds a bundle from the subject declaration, cited requirements, the example, and terms. It also covers `{test}` and `{impl}` owner nodes and checks that distant or non-leaving edges are excluded.\n- `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs` checks which edges contribute, for requirement, example, and parent subjects.\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` and `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` cover anchor contributions. The first asserts the exact input list. The second asserts that only the selected node is supplied.\n- `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes` covers markdown, plain-text, and fixme contributions.\n- `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` covers staging behaviour for declarations, sources, and terms.\n- The citation, site, and book-commentary subjects are covered in `src/authoring/mod.rs`. For the citation and site subjects, tests assert the mandatory input shape.\n\n**Deduplication of identical selections**\n- `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` repeats the same cite and the same term. It asserts exactly one input each for the declaration, the term, and the built-in, and `inputs.len() == 5`.\n- `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` asserts that the recorded `fn[ready]` input appears once.\n\n**Unresolvable inputs reported before inference**\n- `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation` and `unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference` cover a missing file, a missing node, and a disallowed path. They assert a `PermissionDenied` error that names the path.\n- `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` covers a path outside the project.\n- `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` is an end-to-end test. The CLI exits nonzero and reports the path. The model endpoint is never contacted, and the evidence file is unchanged. This also covers the abort-before-model-request and no-evidence-write obligations that the cited `read_denial.mandatory` requires.\n- `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` and `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` show that only current mandatory inputs matter and that old evidence is not carried forward.\n\n**Complete set in the initial request**\n- `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` asserts that the prompt contains the item hash, the cited requirement, and the built-in text.\n- `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` asserts that the subject message equals the template filled with the mandatory inputs.\n- `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` asserts that the requirement, definition, test source, and fixme text are in the first request, and that implementation source is absent.\n\n**Generated `evidence/` handling**\n- `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` covers four cases. The default omits the anchor, and a symlink alias is also omitted. An explicit allow includes the file. An explicit disallow aborts with `PermissionDenied`.\n- `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` covers discovery of references under `evidence/`, with and without an allow.\n\n**Obligation not tested here**\n- The obligation that a contributing requirement must cite this requirement and define its contributions is a book-text obligation. It is carried by the contributing requirements' own text and is not assessed here.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behaviour that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "a315cbacf8e0c5292dd4fa81a25ceab1108709e6c82fb5b24d3c92cd879d021d",
